# --- Output Management ---
# Format: website_creator_title.ext
# Note: %(extractor_key)s is the website (e.g., Youtube),
# %(uploader)s is the creator, and %(title)s is the content.
-o "%(extractor_key)s_%(uploader)s_%(title)s.%(ext)s"

# Restrict filenames to ASCII and replace spaces with underscores
# (Better for shell scripting and terminal navigation)
#--restrict-filenames

# --- Video Quality & Format ---
# Merge into mkv or mp4 (mkv is generally more robust for Linux/FFmpeg)
--merge-output-format mkv

# Prefer high quality but prioritize free formats (VP9/AV1/WebM)
--prefer-free-formats

# --- Metadata & Subtitles ---
# Write metadata to the file (helpful for local media players)
--add-metadata
--embed-subs
--embed-thumbnail

# Download English subtitles or auto-generated ones if available
--write-subs
--write-auto-subs
--sub-langs "en.*"

# --- Performance & Reliability ---
# Use concurrent fragments for faster downloads (standard is 1)
--concurrent-fragments 5

# Continue partially downloaded files
--continue

# Ignore errors (useful for large playlists so one dead link doesn't stop the script)
--ignore-errors
# --- Cookies (Workaround for age-restricted/premium content) ---
#--cookies-from-browser firefox
--user-agent "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/146.0.0.0 Safari/537.36"
##--impersonate Chrome
